  "question": {
    "text": "If <math><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is a non-zero polynomial of degree four, having local extreme points at <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>;</mo></math> then the set <math><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>}</mo></math> contains exactly"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Two irrational and two rational numbers",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Four rational numbers",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Two irrational and one rational number",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Four irrational numbers",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> has extreme points at <math><mo>{</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#39;</mi></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>&#160;</mi></math> at <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>'</mi></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8757;</mo><mi>f</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> is a polynomial</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8747;</mo><mi>a</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>C</mi></math></p><p>Now the equation,</p><p><math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>}</mo><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Hence, the set contains two irrational and one rational number.</p>"
  }
